<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/2nd-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Mobei</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">119 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-xiongnu-war">Han–Xiongnu War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Mobei was fought in 119 BCE north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gobi-desert">Gobi Desert</a> between the armies of Han <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wei-qing">Wei Qing</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huo-qubing">Huo Qubing</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu</a>. The Han cavalry drove the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chanyu">chanyu</a> Yizhixie into flight and inflicted heavy losses, pushing the Xiongnu away from the Chinese frontier. It was the culmination of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-wu-of-han">Emperor Wu</a>'s offensives and began the long Xiongnu decline.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-mobei.jpg" alt="Battle of Mobei" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rob Oo from NL · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:See_the_world_in_one_glance_(49886044227).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
